      "writtenOn": "2020-11-09T18:59:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the report, we\u0027re observing the test failure, too.  Will McVicker is chasing; Friday we identified that the corresponding routines were removed from the compat vdso recently.  Stay tuned.  It looks like SIGBUS is triggered by the `svc` instruction, though it\u0027s not clear yet what\u0027s wrong with the alignment of operands or the instruction itself.\n\n(There might also potentially be a linker flag that GCC was passing to the linker that we need to manually specify. Building with `-v` added to the `VDSO_LDFLAGS` and comparing the flags before/after this change would illuminate such differences).",
      "parentUuid": "32b12aa8_c8aa1c3b",
      "revId": "ee753b7d136d7ac274743983af33b4e5f799d7b4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
